            <ArticleTitle>Stochastic Thermodynamics of Learning.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>010601</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.118.010601</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Virtually every organism gathers information about its noisy environment and builds models from those data, mostly using neural networks. Here, we use stochastic thermodynamics to analyze the learning of a classification rule by a neural network. We show that the information acquired by the network is bounded by the thermodynamic cost of learning and introduce a learning efficiency η≤1. We discuss the conditions for optimal learning and analyze Hebbian learning in the thermodynamic limit.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
